^SERIES = GSE246308
!Series_title = Genomic regions occupied by both RARα and VDR are involved in the convergence and cooperation of retinoid and vitamin D signaling pathways.
!Series_geo_accession = GSE246308
!Series_status = Public on Dec 31 2024
!Series_submission_date = Oct 26 2023
!Series_last_update_date = Apr 15 2025
!Series_pubmed_id = 40167329
!Series_summary = In this study, the retinoid and vitamin D pathways were investigated in PMA-differentiated THP-1 cells treated with or without the RARa agonist, AM580, and/or the VDR agonist, 1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D3 (1,25-vitD or calcitriol), using global approaches. Binding regions of RARa and VDR were determined in PMA-differentiated THP-1 cells using chromatin immunoprecipitation coupled with high-throughput sequencing (ChIP-seq). The gene sets regulated by AM580 and/or 1,25-vitD were identified by RNA-sequencing (RNA-seq). The activity of the regulatory regions was determined by MED1 (a subunit of the Mediator complex) ChIP-seq and chromatin openness was measured using assay for transposase-accessible chromatin with sequencing (ATAC-seq). 
!Series_overall_design = THP1 cells were stimulated with 20 nM PMA for 16 hours. In the case of RARa and VDR ChIP-seq samples: PMA-differentiated THP-1 cells were treated with vehicle (DMSO:EtOH), RARa agonist (100 nM AM580) or VDR agonist (100 nM calcitriol or 1,25-vitD) for 1 hour. Two replicates of each condition were analyzed by ChIP-seq. In the case of MED1 ChIP-seq samples: PMA-differentiated THP-1 cells were treated with vehicle (DMSO:EtOH), RARa agonist (100 nM AM580) and/or VDR agonist (100 nM calcitriol or 1,25-vitD) for 2 hour. Three replicates of each condition were analyzed by ChIP-seq. 
!Series_type = Genome binding/occupancy profiling by high throughput sequencing
